agent/dist/

# local, gitignored env files with real tokens.
#
# The GLOB, not the three bare names it replaced (D-170). Every one of these
# files is edited by hand on a real workstation, and the reflex before editing
# a file full of tokens is to copy it: `cp deploy/ccrc.env deploy/ccrc.env.bak`.
# The bare names ignored the original and left the copy UNTRACKED-BUT-VISIBLE,
# one `git add -A` away from publishing every secret in it — in a repo that is
# public. Measured 2026-08-22: the backup was written, and caught only because
# something else prompted a `git check-ignore`.
#
# The `!` lines are why the glob is safe: the committed .example placeholders
# carry no secrets and MUST stay tracked (boot refuses the unedited mail-token
# placeholder by name, so its absence would be a different failure).
# UNANCHORED on purpose (D-196). These were `deploy/…` globs, which is where the
# files actually live — and that is exactly why it was wrong: a pattern with a
# slash matches ONE directory, so `ccrc.env` at the repo root, `server/ccrc.env`,
# or a copy inside any subdirectory was publishable while looking covered. A
# pattern with no slash matches the NAME at any depth, which is the property
# wanted: these names are never safe, wherever they appear.
ccrc.env*
ccrc-agent.env*
agent.env*
ccrc-mail.token*
exposure.env*
.env*
!*.example

# The reference fleet's concrete values (addresses, user, key names) — the
# Stage 5 sweep rewrote the tree to speak roles, and this operator-only file
# is where the real values went so operations lose nothing (plan Task 8).
deploy/reference-fleet.md

# Local harness configuration. Was protected only by .git/info/exclude, which is
# per-clone and travels with nobody — so the protection did not survive a fork.
.claude/

# migration working artifacts
.extraction/

# session tooling state this box generates in live checkouts
.claude/worktrees/
.worktrees/
.superpowers/
.remember/

# safety net: server/test/boot.test.ts's sensitivity control writes a
# mutated copy of index.ts here (relative imports require it live beside
# its siblings), always removed in a finally block — this is a backstop
# for an interrupted run, not the normal cleanup path.
server/src/__boot_control_mutant__.ts

# tsc's incremental cache — machine-local, and the committed copy had gone stale
# (29 of its 62 recorded roots no longer existed).
*.tsbuildinfo
